    dict(key='17-act-5-figure', kind='figure', title='Before and after a wrong change to the zone file',
         body='wrong_record',
         narration="The last demo starts a second server, with one wrong line. [[slnc 400]] Before the change, the zone gives the store's real address, and the server serves it. [[slnc 600]] After the change, someone has written one nine two dot zero dot two dot six six, with a time to live of eighty six thousand four hundred seconds. [[slnc 300]] The server serves it the same way. [[slnc 300]] It cannot tell a wrong line from a right one. [[slnc 600]] Eighty six thousand four hundred seconds, divided by sixty, and by sixty again, is twenty four hours. One day. [[slnc 300]] Our cache cuts it to sixty seconds, but a resolver without a limit keeps the wrong address for a day. [[slnc 600]] So the protection is around the file: who may change it, review of changes, and short times to live."),
